keywords:
  - Lotka-Volterra systems
  - Darboux polynomials
  - superintegrable systems
  - graphic arrangements
  - spanning trees
abstract: "Proof of van der Kamp's Conjecture 12 (nonisomorphic trees are not LV-equivalent, for generic parameters) in a one-sided form: a generic system of one tree family is never linearly conjugate to any system of the family of a nonisomorphic tree. The all-parameter extension fails. Also: the complete linear Darboux list with an exact genericity condition, all Lotka-Volterra coordinate presentations (spanning trees of the cone over the tree), their symmetry quotient and counts for paths and caterpillars, a recognition test and transfer to Kahan maps. Unrefereed candidate. Original code is MIT-licensed; see LICENSES.md."
